    "note": {
      "id": "1a9a51d9-4531-4ced-b7ef-41865fee28c6",
      "paper_id": "c09db6eb-c617-46a7-a198-9a4b03968429",
      "body": "S899 denominator correction requested by Abdel on 2026-07-28. Training exposure is not used because the paper did not observe practice athlete-exposures: it assumed 40 practices per athlete per year based on investigator and university-staff estimates. The active extraction therefore excludes training count/rate, total exposure, overall incidence, and the duplicated overall concussion/head incidence rows that depend on the training-inclusive denominator. Match count and match incidence are retained. Competition exposure was reconstructed by the authors from preseason rosters and public NCAA schedules rather than an assumed number of events, although it still does not verify individual participation and should be interpreted cautiously. Descriptive concussion totals, sex-specific counts, contact mechanisms, recurrent events, and structured prevalence counts remain because they do not depend on the estimated training denominator. The source sex-count discrepancy remains unresolved: total n=2471; stated sex-available n=2366; results male/female n=1240/1162; Table 1 female n=1204.",
      "created_at": "2026-07-28T17:32:19.732+00:00"
    },
